# Copy to .env (or .env.local) and fill in. Both files are git-ignored.

# ── KruAI mentor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NO VITE_ PREFIX, deliberately. Vite only exposes VITE_* to the browser
# bundle, and this key must stay server-side — it is read by
# server/chat-handler.ts through the dev plugin and by the Vercel function in
# production. Prefixing it to "fix" a missing key would ship it to every
# student's browser.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These two ARE prefixed, because they are meant to reach the browser. The
# publishable/anon key is a public identifier, not a secret: it can do nothing
# on its own, because every table is protected by the row level security
# policies in supabase/migrations. Never put the service_role / secret key
# here — that one bypasses RLS entirely.
#
# Both are on: dashboard → Project Settings → API keys.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Accepted alias for VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — same value, and the name the
# dashboard actually uses for it. Set one or the other, not both.
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /api/chat verifies the caller's Supabase access token before spending any
# Gemini budget, and it needs the project URL to fetch the signing keys. On
# Vercel it reads VITE_SUPABASE_URL above, since every project variable is in
# the function runtime regardless of prefix — so normally nothing more is
# needed. Set this only to point verification at a different project.
# SUPABASE_URL=
#
# Only for a legacy project still signing tokens with the shared HS256 secret.
# This one has NO VITE_ prefix on purpose: it is a real secret, and prefixing
# it would inline it into every student's browser bundle. Projects on
# asymmetric signing keys (the default now, and what this project uses) do not
# need it at all — verification fetches the public JWKS instead.
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
